  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The desk serves both booked readers and walk-ins, and staff can divide its working time into short service blocks.\", \"decision\": \"How should walk-ins share the pickup desk with booked readers?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nStaff begin each service block with the longer waiting group, whether booked readers or walk-ins. Service follows the greater current wait instead of a fixed group order.\nStaff reserve an initial portion of each service block for booked readers and use the remainder for walk-ins. Booked arrivals have predictable access while walk-ins use the continuing spare time.\nStaff alternate short service blocks between booked readers and walk-ins at the pickup desk. Both groups receive a regular turn even when the other group is busy."
    }
  ],
